The most important observation in 114 is:
Flattening is not just traversing preorder. It is also rewiring the existing pointers so the preorder sequence becomes a right-only chain.

Final memory trick
The required order is:
Root → Left → Right


Two ways to obtain it:
Option 1:
Visit preorder and link nodes as you go.

Option 2:
Process reverse preorder:
Right → Left → Root
and link each node to prev.


Your provided code is already an excellent optimal solution in time complexity: \(O(n)\) time and \(O(h)\) recursion space. Use the Morris-style implementation when you need \(O(1)\) auxiliary space.
